# M3U bridge: divert module 31's node-action classification call to
# the hook trampoline at the base of the module 31 segment extension
# payload (composition: work/mod31_compose/mod31_compose.md). This
# scratch copy re-pins the branch target from the withdrawn module 0
# extension placement (0x03079C14, live runtime workspace) to the
# module 31 extension; the site, the displaced instruction and the
# trampoline contract are unchanged from the original 0040.
name: m3u-browser-hook
kind: module
module: 31
region: code
address: 0x0307DF1A
gate: Do NOT stack alone. Requires the module 31 segment extension
  build (--grow 31:code: with the composed payload at
  work/mod31_compose/payload.bin): trampoline at exec 0x0307EE48,
  bridge entry m3u_bridge_node_action at 0x0307EE88. If the payload
  layout changes, regenerate the replacement bytes by assembling
  B.W to the trampoline base at the site address (the composition
  build emits them as build/site40.bin). With the bridge declining
  (non-M3U node, FS type 3 volume, unresolvable or over-cap
  playlist), the patched firmware is behaviour-identical to stock:
  the trampoline's no-match path reproduces the displaced call
  exactly.
expect: fff76df9
replace: 00f095bf
rationale: The site is the single BL inside module 31's node-action
  function 0x0307DEB8 that dispatches on the selected node's class
  byte: stock bytes fff76df9 = BL 0x0307D1F8, executed with
  r0 = r5 = class byte (read from node +0x4E at 0x0307DF06),
  r4 = node pointer, r7 = browser state, r8 = play context
  0x03023980. No BL precedes it in the function, so lr still holds
  the function caller's return address. The replacement 00f095bf =
  B.W 0x0307EE48 enters the payload trampoline, which (1) tests the
  node's 8.3 extension at node +0x57..+0x59 for "M3U", (2) on no
  match calls 0x0307D1F8 with the original argument and resumes
  stock flow at 0x0307DF1E (the instruction after the displaced BL)
  with every register the stock continuation reads in its stock
  state, and (3) on match calls the bridge entry at 0x0307EE88 and,
  if the bridge reports the node handled, leaves through the
  function's own common exit at 0x0307E0C8 (add sp, #0x4C; pop.w)
  with r0 = 1, the same value the stock folder-play success path
  sets at 0x0307E0C6. The trampoline (64 bytes, filling its slot
  exactly at this placement, assembled with rz-asm and audited
  instruction by instruction against its Capstone decode in the
  composition build) preserves
  all callee-saved registers and balances its own push/pop on both
  paths. .m3u8 long-name files are not matched by the SFN test; they
  fall through to stock until the LFN field is pinned.
